# A hidden helper declared twice with values that may disagree (#125): {x: 2}
# makes v1_0._h 2 & 1, an error. It is evaluated, and v1_0.b reads it, so the
# one-value-per-path rule covers it as it does a data field.
-- source.cue --
x: int32
-- target.cue --
b!: int64
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {
	_h: v0_0.x
	_h: 1
	b:  _h + 1
}
-- out --
not total
v1_0._h is written as v0_0.x and as 1, and the two unify, so one may reject the other's value; write the field once (rule write-conflict) @ lens.cue:3:2
